---
title: Guest cancels, commission follows the refund, the host refund is tracked (DEC-018 revised, DEC-024)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor G as Guest
    participant A as Django API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    actor H as Host
    actor M as Admin
    G->>A: GET /me/bookings/{booking_id}/cancellation-preview
    A-->>G: refund 31,750 DZD (50% window of 55,500 + cleaning 4,000)
    G->>A: POST /me/bookings/{booking_id}/cancel
    A->>DB: status cancelled, refund line 31,750
    A->>DB: commission_reversal = apply_bp(6,660, 5,000) = 3,330 back to the host wallet
    Note over A,DB: BLADUS keeps 3,330 DZD
    A->>DB: refund obligation open, due in 7 days, memo refund_due 31,750
    A-)H: you owe the guest 31,750 DZD by the due date
    H->>A: POST /host/refunds/{refund_id}/declare-paid (payment reference)
    alt guest received it
        G->>A: POST /me/refunds/{refund_id}/confirm-received
        A->>DB: settled, memo refund_settled
    else guest did not receive it
        G->>A: POST /me/refunds/{refund_id}/dispute
        A->>DB: disputed (the due date does not move)
        M->>A: GET /admin/refunds?overdue=true
        M->>A: POST /admin/refunds/{refund_id}/settle (note, optional proof)
    end
    Note over H,DB: while a refund is overdue the host has no instant booking and cannot accept requests
